1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:14,764
THE FIRST QUEST REVEAL

2
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:16,891
The first quest will unlock now.

3
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:19,978
Your first quest is…

4
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:22,230
the sunrise

5
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:24,983
from Taebaeksan Mountain.

6
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:25,900
What?

7
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:27,902
WATCHING THE SUNRISE FROM TAEBAEKSAN

8
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:29,195
…from Taebaeksan Mountain.

9
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:30,572
What?

10
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:33,450
The sunrise?

11
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:34,784
What do you mean?

12
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:38,913
TAEBAEKSAN MOUNTAIN

13
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:42,792
1,567 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL
AT THE HEART OF BAEKDUDAEGAN

14
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:46,421
THE HOME OF VARIOUS ALPINE PLANTS

15
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:50,091
THE MOST FAMOUS SNOWY LANDSCAPE IN KOREA

16
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:53,636
AND ONE OF THE MOST POPULAR SUNRISE SPOTS

17
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:58,016
VISITED BY MANY HIKERS

18
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:03,021
DESCEND CLUB'S FIRST QUEST

19
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:07,108
WATCH THE SUNRISE FROM TAEBAEKSAN

20
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:10,945
That means we must wake up
by 5:00 a.m. at the latest.

21
00:01:11,029 --> 00:01:12,572
THE HIKE IS IN TWO DAYS

22
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:14,324
-Maybe even earlier?
-Not by five.

23
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:16,701
By 6:00 or 7:00 a.m.,

24
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:19,037
-We must be up there.
-we should already be up there.

25
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:20,830
SUNRISE IS AT 7:37 A.M.

26
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:24,417
I think we should start hiking
by 5:00 a.m., at the latest.

27
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:26,878
We have both good news and bad news.

28
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,380
-We'll hear the bad news first.
-Bad news.

29
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:32,342
From your accommodation to Taebaeksan,

30
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:34,552
it takes about two and a half hours.

31
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:35,929
It takes so long.

32
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,640
Then we shouldn't sleep at all.

33
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:42,352
We calculated the time and decided
to go to bed at 8:00 p.m. tomorrow.

34
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:44,312
-What?
-We'll go to bed at 8:00 p.m.

35
00:01:44,395 --> 00:01:45,522
What time do we wake up?

36
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:46,815
-At 2:00 a.m.
-What?

37
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:47,982
WAKE UP AT 2:00 A.M.!

38
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:49,984
-Okay.
-What's the good news?

39
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:54,072
The time it takes to go up and down
is very short.

40
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:55,406
Less than four hours.

41
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:58,034
4 HOURS ROUND TRIP

42
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,954
THAT'S GOOD NEWS?

43
00:02:01,037 --> 00:02:03,248
We don't do this even when going fishing.

44
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:04,999
What's wrong with you?

45
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:05,917
LOL

46
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,169
BUT THERE'S A BENEFIT

47
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:10,338
We have a badge system.

48
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:12,841
Do you know how many kilometers
you walked today?

49
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,134
About 12 km?

50
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:15,802
A round trip of 17 km.

51
00:02:15,885 --> 00:02:19,055
A ROUND TRIP OF 17 KM

52
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:22,517
<i>According to the kilometers you walk,</i>

53
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,477
<i>we'll give you kilometer badges.</i>

54
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:29,315
THEY GOT 17 KM FROM THE SEORAKSAN HIKE

55
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:32,902
Then does that lead to… this?

56
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:34,404
I wonder what.

57
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:35,321
Maybe a bonus.

58
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,073
Something like prize money.

59
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:38,700
So you want money?

60
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,535
Of course. You don't like it?

61
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:43,121
I want to be on <i>Three Meals a Day.</i>

62
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:44,956
IT'S BETTER THAN THAT

63
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:48,376
If you reach 50 km,
you'll get 11.25 g of gold.

64
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:50,378
And if you reach 100 km,

65
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:52,755
you'll get a gold badge and a prize.

66
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:55,842
The right to change the theme
of our show as you like.

67
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:57,093
SHOW CHANGE PRIVILEGES

68
00:02:57,176 --> 00:03:00,638
Hey, instead of Taebaeksan,
let's hike Seoraksan four more times.

69
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:03,057
INTRIGUED

70
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:05,894
If you reach 100 km,
you can discuss among yourselves,

71
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:09,606
and if you decide that hiking
is not right for you, you can quit it

72
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:10,648
and change the theme.

73
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:11,983
SENSATIONAL OFFER

74
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:13,735
You'll have that right.

75
00:03:13,818 --> 00:03:15,778
Avatar Blind Date is fun. Want to do it?

76
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:16,779
HIS CONTENT ON YOUTUBE

77
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:18,448
We can just sit

78
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:20,825
and give instructions
via a radio. It's so fun.

79
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:21,951
PLUGGING HIS OWN CONTENT

80
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,286
Honestly, I really enjoyed it.

81
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:24,829
Right? It's really fun.

82
00:03:26,998 --> 00:03:28,458
Hey, but 100 km is…

83
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:29,959
To reach 100 km,

84
00:03:30,043 --> 00:03:32,879
we have to hike like today
five or six more times.

85
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:33,796
Right…

86
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,634
THEY END THE MEAL FEELING DOWN

87
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:40,470
MOVING TO THEIR ACCOMMODATION BY BUS

88
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:42,263
TAKE A HIKE!

89
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:43,389
My legs…

90
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:44,933
My legs hurt so much.

91
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,894
Oh, God.

92
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:50,521
Geez.

93
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:51,606
GRUNTS

94
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:53,024
Gosh, the stairs.

95
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:56,653
Gosh, climbing the bus stairs
felt like hiking.

96
00:03:57,695 --> 00:03:59,906
HEADING TO THEIR ACCOMMODATION
WHILE GROANING

97
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:02,325
Seriously.

98
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:04,953
I respect the directors so much.

99
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:06,496
I mean it. Geez.

100
00:04:06,579 --> 00:04:07,705
They're so cool.

101
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:10,667
After all that, they're still filming.

102
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,001
Seriously, I…

103
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:15,421
I can't complain in front of them.

104
00:04:15,505 --> 00:04:17,215
I mean, I already did, but…

105
00:04:18,132 --> 00:04:20,718
My closest friend these days

106
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,762
is a camera director.

107
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:26,307
Whenever he works abroad,
he goes running all the time.

108
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,394
I thought, "What a good job he has."

109
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:31,104
But I changed my mind today.

110
00:04:32,146 --> 00:04:34,941
All the camera directors
across the country,

111
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:36,526
you have my respect.

112
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:39,821
Will you shower and go to bed right away?

113
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:41,948
Maybe we should eat something?

114
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:44,993
My blood sugar's low, so I think I'll have

115
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:47,745
some sweet cake, fruit, or snacks
before going to bed.

116
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:50,790
PASSED OUT

117
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:53,668
SNORING

118
00:04:53,751 --> 00:04:55,503
SNORING

119
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:59,215
AFTER 30 MINUTES OF SNORING

120
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,259
GOSEONG-GUN
TOSEONG-MYEON

121
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:05,638
THEY ARRIVE AT THEIR ACCOMMODATION

122
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:11,644
We're here.

123
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,441
You guys snored like…

124
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:17,483
Like crazy, right?

125
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:20,236
-I thought it was a dream. Was it real?
-They snored like…

126
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:22,989
I thought I was dreaming.

127
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,742
GROANING

128
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,118
GROANING

129
00:05:27,201 --> 00:05:30,204
BARELY CLIMBING DOWN THE BUS

130
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:32,957
Wow…

131
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,126
-It's nice.
-What a nice house.

132
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:36,919
We're staying at such a nice place?

133
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:40,381
DESCEND CLUB'S FIRST BASE CAMP

134
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:45,261
SEORAKSAN
ACCOMMODATION

135
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,681
RIGHT IN FRONT OF BLUE GOSEONG SEA

136
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:55,021
IT WILL WASH AWAY THE FATIGUE
FROM THE TOUGH HIKE

137
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:57,190
What is this place?

138
00:05:58,191 --> 00:05:59,525
Why is it so nice?

139
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:01,736
THEIR FIRST COZY SPACE

140
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:09,202
I'll sleep on the couch right away.

141
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:11,871
There are two beds.

142
00:06:11,954 --> 00:06:13,498
THE SPACE THEY'LL REST IN

143
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:14,499
BIG BEDROOM

144
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:16,375
SMALL BEDROOM

145
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:19,170
What? We can all sleep here.

146
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,088
VERY SATISFIED

147
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:21,214
This is so nice.

148
00:06:21,297 --> 00:06:22,882
I want to sleep there.

149
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:25,176
ARGUING OVER THE ROOMS

150
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:26,761
They'll be uncomfortable.

151
00:06:26,844 --> 00:06:28,471
Why don't you use that room?

152
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,890
I'll feel more comfortable
in the living room.

153
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:32,558
You know, I really…

154
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:34,519
My snoring is really terrible.

155
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:36,229
VOLUNTEERS TO SLEEP IN THE LIVING ROOM

156
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:37,814
BIG BEDROOM
CHAE-MIN & TARZZAN

157
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:39,774
SMALL BEDROOM
DOWOON

158
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:42,985
-The convenience store's right outside.
-Right.

159
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:47,281
THEY HEAD TO THE CONVENIENCE STORE
FOR SNACKS

160
00:06:47,365 --> 00:06:49,534
When we left after the barbecue,

161
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:52,453
it was so cold
that I can still remember it.

162
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:55,123
What was the shelter called again?

163
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:56,082
Huiun…

164
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:58,000
No, Huimun?

165
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:58,918
What was it?

166
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:00,628
-What was it?
-Huimun… Hui…

167
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:02,547
IT'S AT THE TIP OF THEIR TONGUE

168
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:03,464
Hui…

169
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:04,382
Huijeong?

170
00:07:04,465 --> 00:07:05,925
-Huijeonggak!
-Is it?

171
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:09,804
"Huijeonggak" sounds like
some very nice Chinese restaurant.

172
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:10,847
What was it?

173
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:13,683
Was it Hoichungwon? What was it?

174
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:15,268
Hoichungwon Observatory?

175
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:17,353
Hui… Huijungdae?

176
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,188
I think it was something like that.

177
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,690
You'll see when it's aired.

178
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:22,442
…THE FORGOTTEN HUIUNGAK SHELTER

179
00:07:23,234 --> 00:07:24,235
-Hello.
-Hello.

180
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:26,863
Sweets are here.
And we need snacks for tomorrow.

181
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,114
Green grape candy's the best.

182
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:29,782
Then should we buy this?

183
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:31,451
Yes, we can all share this one.

184
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:32,368
Let's do that.

185
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:33,619
BUYING SNACKS FOR TAEBAEKSAN

186
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:35,121
And one more for tomorrow…

187
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:36,414
The day after tomorrow, right?

188
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:37,623
Oh, you're right.

189
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:38,875
My heart almost sank.

190
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,294
GIVEN ONE MORE DAY TO LIVE

191
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,212
Now, let's buy what we'll eat now.

192
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:46,174
I've felt hungry all day today.

193
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:47,758
CONSTANTLY FEELING HUNGRY

194
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:49,093
What should we eat?

195
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:50,511
Wow, there's ice cream.

196
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:52,013
Should we buy it too?

197
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:53,514
Gosh, ice cream…

198
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:54,432
Vanilla flavor…

199
00:07:54,515 --> 00:07:55,516
CAN'T RESIST SWEET TREATS

200
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,434
And I crave…

201
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:58,311
CHECKING OUT THE BREAD SECTION

202
00:07:58,394 --> 00:08:00,146
Having this with milk is so good.

203
00:08:00,229 --> 00:08:01,355
You know, right?

204
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:02,899
Be honest.

205
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:04,400
-Is that good for you?
-Come on.

206
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:09,155
You're the most enthusiastic
I've seen today.

207
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,114
It'll be so good.

208
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:13,409
I'll pay and send you the amount later.
Let's go Dutch.

209
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,620
MANAGER CAR PAYS WITHOUT HESITATION

210
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:17,038
It feels like we're on a trip.

211
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:19,582
What's the theme of the show?

212
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:20,666
Our show?

213
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,835
It's about hiking.

214
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:23,836
Do you like hiking?

215
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,754
No.

216
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:27,089
-See?
-We don't either.

217
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:29,300
We went hiking in Seoraksan
in this weather.

218
00:08:29,383 --> 00:08:30,343
That's not right.

219
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:32,720
-See?
-Did you hear that? It's crazy.

220
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:33,888
HE'S ON THEIR SIDE

221
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:36,265
Have you watched <i>2 Days & 1 Night?</i>

222
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:37,183
Yes.

223
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:40,061
The one who produced that show
is the producer of this show.

224
00:08:40,144 --> 00:08:40,978
Mr. Nah Yung-suk.

225
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,230
Yes, that Mr. Nah.

226
00:08:42,313 --> 00:08:45,316
made us hike Seoraksan
in this cold weather.

227
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:47,652
FIRST PERSON SYMPATHIZING WITH HIM

228
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:51,656
In <i>2 Days & 1 Night</i>, they go into water.
But you didn't do that, did you?

229
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:54,367
EVERYONE: SILENT

230
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:56,035
Then they're going easy on you.

231
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:57,745
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

232
00:08:57,828 --> 00:08:59,080
-Bye.
-Thank you.

233
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,085
I think we can eat here.

234
00:09:04,168 --> 00:09:05,253
Yes, let's eat here.

235
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:08,005
A MODEST SNACK PARTY

236
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:09,799
I feel so happy just being inside a house.

237
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,429
NOTICING

238
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:16,514
LAUGHING

239
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:18,099
He keeps spacing out.

240
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:19,976
Is it good?

241
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:21,310
I'm so tired.

242
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:24,522
I expected it,
but it was harder than I thought.

243
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:27,942
It felt like a battle of mental strength
at the end.

244
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:31,153
It felt so frustrating
when it was almost over.

245
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:33,239
That was when the battle began.

246
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:36,200
For me, it was better
when we were climbing up

247
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:37,910
-than the last part.
-Right.

248
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,496
Watching for rocks and being careful,

249
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,415
it was somewhat fun.

250
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:44,333
After that, I started to loosen up

251
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:46,419
and was like, "When does it end?"

252
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:48,546
Even after we saw the Buddha statue,

253
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:49,714
it was a long way to go.

254
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:51,591
Right, I was so shocked.

255
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:54,635
<i>Seriously, I thought we'd reach</i>
<i>the parking lot soon.</i>

256
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:56,762
<i>But it wasn't there.</i>

257
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:57,722
<i>Seriously.</i>

258
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:59,640
COMING BACK DOWN FELT NEVER-ENDING

259
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:02,602
If you get an offer for a hiking movie,
what will you do?

260
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:03,728
Seoraksan?

261
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:04,937
The title is "Seoraksan."

262
00:10:06,063 --> 00:10:07,231
A SUDDEN "WHAT IF" GAME

263
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:09,317
And you have a feeling it'll hit big.

264
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:13,779
But you have to hike it like today,
eight more times to film it.

265
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:17,450
And since you're a rescue worker,
you have to carry people for real.

266
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:20,578
HE THOROUGHLY EXPLAINS THE DETAILS

267
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:22,246
I should do it.

268
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,040
-Wow.
-Gosh, so professional.

269
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:25,374
-He's professional.
-Right.

270
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:31,047
CRUNCHING

271
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,173
Should we go to bed?

272
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,091
Yes, let's go to bed.

273
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,344
I'll sleep on the floor.

274
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:37,720
No, I will.

275
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:39,263
No, no.

276
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:40,306
LATE-NIGHT BED BATTLE

277
00:10:40,389 --> 00:10:42,433
I think I'll wake up first, so…

278
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:44,101
No.

279
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,853
-What?
-No, you can't.

280
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:47,188
-Why not?
-I…

281
00:10:48,564 --> 00:10:52,360
BOTH TRY TO TAKE THE FLOOR

282
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:54,445
No, please. You can't.

283
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:56,489
-Rock-paper-scissors, then?
-Okay.

284
00:10:56,572 --> 00:10:57,740
Winner takes what?

285
00:10:58,282 --> 00:10:59,283
Winner takes…

286
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:00,868
-the floor.
-Okay.

287
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:02,370
-Rock-paper-scissors.
-Scissors.

288
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:03,287
ROCK
ROCK

289
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:04,664
WIN
LOSE

290
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,248
TARZZAN SLEEPS ON THE FLOOR

291
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:07,667
Good night, guys.

292
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,210
-Good night.
-Good night.

293
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:12,254
SEORAKSAN TRAINING ENDS

294
00:11:17,134 --> 00:11:19,428
MORNING COMES

295
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:22,598
TODAY IS A RECOVERY DAY

296
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:25,017
CURRENT TIME

297
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,313
CHAE-MIN WAKES UP AFTER 12 HOURS OF SLEEP

298
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:31,148
TARZZAN WAKES UP TOO

299
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:33,943
RECOVERY STEP 1
ENOUGH SLEEP

300
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:36,028
Geez!

301
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:37,988
Did you sleep well?

302
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,198
I passed out.

303
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:40,116
STROKING

304
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:41,492
THEY'VE GROWN A LOT CLOSER

305
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,411
-How are you feeling?
-Feeling good.

306
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:44,328
-Good.
-And you?

307
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:45,413
I'm feeling great.

308
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:47,623
-I'm recovered.
-You're young indeed.

309
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:49,583
Are they still sleeping?

310
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:50,626
I think so.

311
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:53,337
Should we go to the first floor
and eat cereal?

312
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:57,967
FEELING HUNGRY UPON WAKING UP

313
00:11:59,093 --> 00:11:59,927
What?

314
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:03,556
I woke up way earlier.

315
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,015
Hey.

316
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:06,642
What? Were you not sleeping?

317
00:12:06,725 --> 00:12:08,894
I went to bed early, you know.

318
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,397
-When did you wake up?
-Around 8:00 a.m.

319
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,314
Really?

320
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:13,941
You were the first to wake up.

321
00:12:14,692 --> 00:12:16,610
I even went downstairs and had <i>ramyeon.</i>

322
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:17,736
What?

323
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,321
What? You already ate?

324
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:21,824
2 HOURS AGO

325
00:12:22,658 --> 00:12:25,661
HE FINISHED A BOWL OF RAMYEON

326
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:28,831
Wow, and here we thought
we were the early birds.

327
00:12:28,914 --> 00:12:30,749
He must be still sleeping, right?

328
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:31,667
Right.

329
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:34,253
DOWOON IS STILL ASLEEP

330
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:37,673
"A Book for Hikers to Read on Mountains."

331
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:39,508
RECOVERY STEP 2
MINDSET TRAINING

332
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:40,426
"Wrong hiking"?

333
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:41,719
WRONG HIKING HARMS YOUR HEALTH

334
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:44,138
That's terrible. A book to read…

335
00:12:44,221 --> 00:12:45,890
20 HIKING HABIT CHECKS

336
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:49,477
"I go hiking for exercise
even though I'm tired from overworking."

337
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:50,603
It's wrong.

338
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:53,481
Isn't that us tomorrow?

339
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:57,067
I think we'll be hiking wrong.

340
00:12:57,568 --> 00:13:00,112
"I often feel dead on my feet."

341
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:01,614
This is too tough.

342
00:13:01,697 --> 00:13:02,656
Careful.

343
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:04,033
Are you okay?

344
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,951
"I sweat profusely when hiking."

345
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,369
You suddenly look ill.

346
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:08,996
You look pale.

347
00:13:09,079 --> 00:13:10,789
"My knees hurt while climbing down."

348
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:12,416
My thighs feel tight already.

349
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,168
Gosh, this is…

350
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:17,922
"After hiking,
I feel completely exhausted."

351
00:13:19,131 --> 00:13:21,300
If at least seven are applicable to you,

352
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:23,886
it means hiking

353
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:25,679
is harming your health.

354
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,599
<i>Gosh, it was really tough yesterday.</i>

355
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:30,684
22 HOURS
BEFORE THE SUNRISE FROM TAEBAEKSAN

356
00:13:31,393 --> 00:13:34,104
KITCHEN, 1ST FLOOR

357
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:36,232
-Are you going to have eggs?
-I should.

358
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:37,233
We need protein.

359
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:39,401
I'm thinking of making French toast,

360
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:40,694
since we have eggs.

361
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:43,781
BREAKFAST IS FRENCH TOAST

362
00:13:43,864 --> 00:13:46,659
WASHING HANDS FIRST

363
00:13:58,712 --> 00:14:01,257
I'm frying eggs in butter,
and it smells so good.

364
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:03,342
Do you like your eggs sunny side up?

365
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:04,843
Totally.

366
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:06,762
A SIDE DISH OF FRIED EGGS, COMPLETE

367
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:09,014
BEATING THE EGGS THOROUGHLY

368
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:11,892
Just soak them with your hand.

369
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:14,937
BOLD MOVE

370
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,063
It looks good.

371
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:17,273
Right?

372
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,316
CUTTING BANANA IN THE MEANTIME

373
00:14:22,861 --> 00:14:25,072
WASHES STRAWBERRIES

374
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:26,574
AND PUTS THEM ON THE BANANA SLICES

375
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:29,076
BRUNCH COMPLETE

376
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:31,036
Look at us two guys…

377
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:31,996
CHORTLES

378
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:33,038
…having brunch.

379
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,585
Wow, this is…

380
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:39,378
We have to take a photo.

381
00:14:39,461 --> 00:14:40,588
This is my first time.

382
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:43,132
PROUD

383
00:14:43,215 --> 00:14:46,135
CHAE-MIN AND TARZZAN'S
PETIT BRUNCH

384
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:48,929
-Thank you for the food.
-Thank you for the food.

385
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:51,724
There are a lot of eggs.

386
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:53,934
It should be more, actually.

387
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:56,228
-Really?
-Yes.

388
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,522
How many eggs do you usually eat?

389
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:01,150
I try to eat 30 g of protein per meal.

390
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:03,152
But there's some egg in the toast too.

391
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:04,486
Right.

392
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:06,697
Hey, my dear friends.

393
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:08,282
I picked up some coffee for you.

394
00:15:08,365 --> 00:15:09,533
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

395
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,243
CARRYING CAREFULLY

396
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:14,371
BUT SPILLING SOME

397
00:15:14,455 --> 00:15:15,915
Hey, do you want to have some?

398
00:15:15,998 --> 00:15:17,583
No, I'm good. I'm full.

399
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:21,754
When do you think Dowoon will wake up?

400
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:22,755
At 4:00 p.m.?

401
00:15:22,838 --> 00:15:24,340
I bet he'll wake up so late.

402
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:25,841
I think he'll wake up…

403
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:28,469
around 1:00 or 2:00 p.m.?

404
00:15:29,094 --> 00:15:30,721
CURRENT TIME

405
00:15:30,804 --> 00:15:32,932
HE DOESN'T LOOK LIKE HE'LL WAKE UP AT ALL

406
00:15:34,683 --> 00:15:36,727
I wish tomorrow
would be relaxing like this.

407
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:41,023
RECOVERY STEP 3
PROTEIN INTAKE

408
00:15:41,106 --> 00:15:41,941
Yes.

409
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,567
CHAE-MIN TAKES A CALL AFTER THE MEAL

410
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,110
Yes, we hiked Seoraksan yesterday.

411
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:47,154
It wasn't easy at all.

412
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,950
I think I just kept climbing up
without talking.

413
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:53,410
No, it was so tough that I couldn't talk.

414
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:57,748
So I passed out around 10:00 p.m.

415
00:15:58,874 --> 00:15:59,959
Who is it?

416
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,126
It's my mother.

417
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:04,630
It'll be too heartbreaking
for her to watch.

418
00:16:05,422 --> 00:16:07,758
No. He says it'll be too heartbreaking
for you to watch.

419
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:08,842
ONE HIKE, INSTANT BAD SON

420
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:11,512
The show title is <i>Take a Hike!</i>
and it's about

421
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:13,681
finding out why we go hiking.

422
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:15,265
CONCEPT: FINDING OUT WHY PEOPLE HIKE

423
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:17,059
But I don't think we'll find out.

424
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:21,438
I think mountains are most beautiful
when we see them from afar.

425
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:22,690
Okay.

426
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:24,108
HE FEELS BETTER THANKS TO MOM

427
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,150
I love you.

428
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:26,652
Sit here.

429
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,613
Who did you pick as the MVP?

430
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:31,031
What about you?

431
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:32,366
Car, of course.

432
00:16:32,449 --> 00:16:33,742
-Why me?
-Me too.

433
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:35,577
I said I was proud of you.

434
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:36,620
That's good.

435
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:39,456
-I said you complained less than expected.
-"I was so proud of him."

436
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:41,792
WHY HE'S MVP:
COMPLAINED LESS THAN EXPECTED

437
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,836
Who do you think the MVP is?

438
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:45,004
Car, the garden.

439
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:48,716
Since he complained
less than I'd expected.

440
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:50,801
It was so tough for him,

441
00:16:50,884 --> 00:16:53,929
but he finished it, and I think
that's what matters the most.

442
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:55,597
I'm younger than him,

443
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:56,724
but I was proud of him.

444
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,143
Today's MVP

445
00:16:59,893 --> 00:17:01,270
is you, Car, the garden.

446
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:05,524
TWO-TIME SEORAKSAN MVP

447
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:06,817
I just put that on.

448
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:07,735
You did?

449
00:17:07,818 --> 00:17:08,652
SLUGGISH

450
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:09,737
It's so dry.

451
00:17:10,487 --> 00:17:12,072
-What? You woke up.
-What?

452
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:13,240
DOWOON WAKES UP

453
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:14,992
You should wash up now.

454
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:18,370
-Foam rollers.
-Hey, how are your legs?

455
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:20,539
DOWOON GRABS A FOAM ROLLER FIRST

456
00:17:21,123 --> 00:17:23,250
Dowoon, put these on.

457
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:25,002
-What are those?
-For your calves.

458
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:27,337
AN ITEM TARZZAN RECOMMENDS: YOGA RINGS

459
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:28,797
On your calves, like this.

460
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,884
-Slide it up to the calf.
-All the way.

461
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:34,636
Actually, you need to walk with them on
to get better.

462
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:37,347
Wait, walk like this?

463
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:41,852
Seriously?

464
00:17:41,935 --> 00:17:44,188
HE LOOKS LIKE A TODDLER LEARNING TO WALK

465
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:45,439
Come on, hurry up.

466
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:51,987
THEY ARE GOOD FRIENDS HELPING HIM WALK

467
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:53,864
-Hey, you woke up.
-Yes.

468
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:55,449
When did you wake up?

469
00:17:56,075 --> 00:17:57,367
-Like this?
-Yes, like that.

470
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:59,244
-Like this?
-Yes, but that looks painful.

471
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,913
Wow, this feels nice too.

472
00:18:00,996 --> 00:18:02,039
INTERESTED

473
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:04,124
GROANS

474
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:05,542
Like this?

475
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:06,877
JUST GOING FOR IT

476
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,920
Yes, up and down.

477
00:18:08,003 --> 00:18:08,837
UP AND DOWN

478
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:09,755
Feels nice, right?

479
00:18:09,838 --> 00:18:11,924
Side rolling is the best, though.

480
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,092
-Like this?
-Yes.

481
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,343
Like that.

482
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:16,929
GROANS

483
00:18:17,012 --> 00:18:18,263
GROANS

484
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,765
Side rolling's so painful.

485
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:21,141
So that's how you do it.

486
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:23,060
-Do some more.
-I think you need it,

487
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:25,187
-or you'll cramp up tomorrow.
-Exactly.

488
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,146
FOAM ROLLER

489
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,564
FOAM PILLOW

490
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:29,191
Isn't this what it's really for?

491
00:18:29,983 --> 00:18:32,152
-I need to do it too.
-Small ones are more painful.

492
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,112
GROANS

493
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:34,363
It's really painful.

494
00:18:34,446 --> 00:18:35,447
Geez.

495
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:39,284
It pisses me off that they prepared them.

496
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:42,913
They set them all up
because they knew we'd have sore muscles.

497
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:46,166
THE STAFF'S FORESIGHT ANGERS HIM

498
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:51,296
RECOVERY STEP 4
MUSCLE RECOVERY COMPLETE

499
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:52,297
CURRENT TIME

500
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,674
<i>-Car.</i>
<i>-Yes?</i>

501
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:55,926
<i>How about we go have some crabs today?</i>

502
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:57,261
<i>Sure, let's do that.</i>

503
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:01,223
Wow, the wind's so strong.

504
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:06,186
-Who should drive?
-I'll do it.

505
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,063
-Why's it so strong?
-It's pushing me.

506
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,648
It's like a disaster movie.

507
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:11,817
-It makes me walk fast.
-I'll ride shotgun.

508
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,235
-Okay, I'll drive.
-Okay.

509
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:14,153
It's so cold.

510
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:16,405
THEY MANAGE TO GET IN

511
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:17,948
Hold on. The door won't close.

512
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:19,032
It's unbelievable.

513
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:22,035
-Seat belts.
-Seat belts, everyone.

514
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:23,078
It's so cold.

515
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:25,289
Hey, just go.

516
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:28,125
FRANTIC

517
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:29,626
Open it just a little.

518
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,795
We'll go ahead of you. You might run off.

519
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:33,922
Why didn't you move faster then?

520
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:35,507
That was close.

521
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:38,844
Do they really suspect we might run off?

522
00:19:38,927 --> 00:19:40,721
I bet, because of me.

523
00:19:40,804 --> 00:19:42,097
HIGHLY LIKELY TO RUN OFF

524
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:44,892
Next time he comes, pretend to stop
and go a little further.

525
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:47,686
HEADING OUT WITH THE ESCAPE TIP

526
00:19:47,769 --> 00:19:51,190
ACCOMMODATION
RESTAURANT

527
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:53,233
I feel comfortable around you guys now.

528
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:54,902
I do, too.

529
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:57,321
It isn't easy
to become comfortable like this.

530
00:19:57,404 --> 00:20:00,574
Honestly, even if we go around
only in our underwear in our room,

531
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:02,701
I don't think it'll feel awkward.

532
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,870
-I slept in only my underwear.
-Really?

533
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:07,247
I saw it.

534
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:09,917
-For real?
-They were black.

535
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:10,918
You're right.

536
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,921
During our first meeting, you said

537
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:16,798
we'd get really close
after our first hike.

538
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:20,844
It was quite awkward
even to call them by their names.

539
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:25,432
But we became like close friends quickly.

540
00:20:25,515 --> 00:20:27,851
I'm not the type
to be on a first-name basis quickly.

541
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:31,980
But maybe because of the hike,
I could easily call Chae-min by his name.

542
00:20:32,064 --> 00:20:34,233
I think some kind
of comradeship was forged.

543
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,401
That's very important, you know?

544
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:39,154
The sea in Goseong is really clear.

545
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:41,990
I came to the beach here last summer.

546
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:44,952
It wasn't crowded,
and the water was so clear.

547
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:45,869
Oh, the sea?

548
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:48,247
I heard the East Sea is beautiful.

549
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:49,248
BEACH, MOUNTAINS, LAKE

550
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:51,833
GOSEONG, WHERE SEA, LAKE,
AND MOUNTAINS MEET

551
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:55,837
I just saw mountains. It's pissing me off.

552
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,005
Sorry, I'll go fast.

553
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:58,048
Mountains over there…

554
00:20:58,131 --> 00:20:59,549
VROOM

555
00:21:00,133 --> 00:21:01,218
Are you flooring it?

556
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:02,135
Yes.

557
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:05,138
It sounds like <i>Mario Kart.</i>

558
00:21:06,306 --> 00:21:08,100
WHILE FLOORING IT

559
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:12,187
THEY ARRIVE AT DONGMYEONG PORT IN SOKCHO

560
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,690
Oh, there's a lot here. Good choice.

561
00:21:14,773 --> 00:21:15,774
-I think.
-Right.

562
00:21:15,857 --> 00:21:18,777
THE CRAB RESTAURANT
CHAE-MIN AND TARZZAN FOUND

563
00:21:21,697 --> 00:21:22,948
Hello.

564
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:24,157
Hello.

565
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:25,826
You can keep your shoes on.

566
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:27,452
Goodness.

567
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,454
What should we have?

568
00:21:30,038 --> 00:21:31,623
-King crab?
-Sure, let's do that.

569
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:33,208
Then, a four-person set of king crab.

570
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:34,126
Good.

571
00:21:34,876 --> 00:21:36,503
I'm hungry now that I'm here.

572
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:38,422
-Right.
-Suddenly…

573
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:43,844
Gosh, I'm in trouble.

574
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:47,931
Look at the crab mustard.

575
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:50,851
KING CRAB

576
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:57,649
-This is bad.
-Thank you for the food.

577
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:58,900
Look at the meat.

578
00:21:59,568 --> 00:22:01,403
-It's so plump.
-Wow.

579
00:22:06,199 --> 00:22:07,451
Let's dig in.

580
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:15,125
-This was a good choice.
-Right.

581
00:22:35,645 --> 00:22:37,898
The king crab meat is so…

582
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,399
This is my first time.

583
00:22:43,361 --> 00:22:45,822
You should dip it into this.

584
00:22:46,406 --> 00:22:47,616
Oh, really?

585
00:22:48,408 --> 00:22:49,409
It's better this way.

586
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:50,702
CRAB MEAT + INNARDS

587
00:22:50,786 --> 00:22:51,661
The crab mustard.

588
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:55,207
AS TARZZAN RECOMMENDED

589
00:22:55,290 --> 00:22:57,793
-It's so savory.
-It's amazing, gosh.

590
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:00,420
What is this? Innards?

591
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:03,048
I think you can just eat it.

592
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:04,424
It's also meat.

593
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:08,345
It's good, wow.

594
00:23:08,845 --> 00:23:10,722
It looks like a crab stick.

595
00:23:11,556 --> 00:23:14,226
BUT IT'S REAL CRAB MEAT

596
00:23:14,309 --> 00:23:16,937
We're eating every meal so passionately.

597
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:17,938
Right.

598
00:23:18,021 --> 00:23:19,189
We should eat well.

599
00:23:19,272 --> 00:23:20,107
Right.

600
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,233
-Is that rice?
-Yes.

601
00:23:21,316 --> 00:23:22,150
Thank you.

602
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:23,276
FOR THE PASSIONATE EATERS

603
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,444
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

604
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:25,570
It looks great.

605
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:26,488
Seriously.

606
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:27,739
CRAB MUSTARD FRIED RICE

607
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:38,750
This is so good too.

608
00:23:43,004 --> 00:23:43,922
Is it good?

609
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:53,515
It's so good with kimchi.

610
00:23:54,975 --> 00:23:56,643
It's so good.

611
00:23:58,436 --> 00:23:59,563
It really is.

612
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:03,358
Instead of wanting to go hiking
while watching our show,

613
00:24:03,441 --> 00:24:05,527
viewers will want to eat the food we eat.

614
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:09,114
You can eat the noodles
if you like them al dente.

615
00:24:09,990 --> 00:24:11,324
Thank you.

616
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:13,201
RED SNOW CRAB RAMYEON

617
00:24:16,204 --> 00:24:18,081
It looks good. It looks perfect now.

618
00:24:29,676 --> 00:24:30,969
I can smell crab.

619
00:24:32,053 --> 00:24:32,888
Is it different?

620
00:24:32,971 --> 00:24:34,598
It tastes like the sea, I'd say.

621
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:43,106
Wow, it is different.

622
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:45,066
I can taste the crab flavor.

623
00:24:49,529 --> 00:24:51,364
My God, the broth is…

624
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:55,202
It's so good.

625
00:24:55,285 --> 00:24:56,745
IT MAKES HIM KEEP EXCLAIMING

626
00:24:56,828 --> 00:24:58,872
It feels like we're besties already.

627
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:00,916
We are, since we ate crab together.

628
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:04,336
You're crab-solutely right.

629
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:09,090
While filming a hiking show,
I thought I'd lose a lot of weight.

630
00:25:09,174 --> 00:25:11,259
-But we're eating so well.
-You're right.

631
00:25:12,135 --> 00:25:14,638
If you make good choices
on food like this, we're happy too.

632
00:25:14,721 --> 00:25:15,972
THE CREW IS HAPPY TOO

633
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:18,850
-That feels more rewarding.
-Since we can eat it too.

634
00:25:18,934 --> 00:25:21,603
Right, because the staff
have to eat what we eat?

635
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:24,606
I think we should think about this.

636
00:25:26,066 --> 00:25:27,567
But if we keep it up,

637
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:30,445
they might be more accepting
when we ask something.

638
00:25:30,528 --> 00:25:31,363
Is that so?

639
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:32,405
We can make a deal.

640
00:25:32,489 --> 00:25:33,865
Give and take?

641
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:35,867
They might lower the difficulty.

642
00:25:35,951 --> 00:25:37,744
They might feel bad.

643
00:25:37,827 --> 00:25:38,870
That's good.

644
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:40,747
You're quite the diplomat.

645
00:25:41,998 --> 00:25:43,583
I tend to do things unilaterally.

646
00:25:44,668 --> 00:25:46,586
We should appoint Chae-min
as our diplomat.

647
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:47,796
DESCEND CLUB'S DIPLOMAT

648
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:50,173
Does a hiking club need a diplomat?

649
00:25:50,257 --> 00:25:52,968
It's important.
When we need to negotiate with them,

650
00:25:53,051 --> 00:25:54,135
your diplomatic attitude…

651
00:25:54,219 --> 00:25:55,637
ESSENTIAL DIPLOMACY SKILLS

652
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:57,430
…will be very crucial. And as for Dowoon…

653
00:25:58,181 --> 00:25:59,599
Appoint him as our driver?

654
00:26:01,142 --> 00:26:04,020
Just "driver" sounds lame.
Let's give him a proper title.

655
00:26:04,104 --> 00:26:06,606
-How about the Minister of Transport?
-Minister of Transport.

656
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:07,649
MINISTER OF TRANSPORT

657
00:26:07,732 --> 00:26:09,317
Foreign Affairs and Transport.

658
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:10,318
Sounds good.

659
00:26:10,402 --> 00:26:11,945
And I'm the Prime Minister.

660
00:26:12,028 --> 00:26:13,446
Then he's the President.

661
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:14,823
PRESIDENT TAR

662
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:18,201
It seems Producer Nah's determined
to put us through a lot,

663
00:26:18,285 --> 00:26:19,577
but I'm anxious

664
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:21,037
because we're eating so well.

665
00:26:22,247 --> 00:26:25,583
I mean, he's known for not giving food
and not letting members sleep.

666
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:26,543
Wait.

667
00:26:26,626 --> 00:26:28,169
If we say things like that,

668
00:26:28,253 --> 00:26:31,214
he might change his mind
and do something like that.

669
00:26:31,298 --> 00:26:32,632
PREVENTING A DIPLOMATIC CRISIS

670
00:26:32,716 --> 00:26:33,550
We made it clear.

671
00:26:33,633 --> 00:26:36,094
If we can't sleep or eat,
we can't do this.

672
00:26:36,177 --> 00:26:37,345
He's diplomatic indeed.

673
00:26:37,429 --> 00:26:40,265
He sure keeps a balance between us.

674
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,517
He's like Zhuge Liang.

675
00:26:43,101 --> 00:26:44,352
Zhuge Liang?

676
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:45,562
CHAE LIANG

677
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:46,938
What are you, then?

678
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:48,982
I'm just a fat man.

679
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:51,276
A fat man.

680
00:26:51,359 --> 00:26:52,193
FAT ZHANG FEI

681
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:54,487
But Jung-won is right about that.

682
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:57,490
I think it's our first time
letting members sleep and eat well.

683
00:26:57,574 --> 00:27:00,785
But not giving us food after hiking?
That would be so…

684
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:04,122
I think it's because
we all hiked together.

685
00:27:04,205 --> 00:27:06,291
If they didn't,
it might've been different.

686
00:27:06,374 --> 00:27:07,542
Since we did it together?

687
00:27:07,625 --> 00:27:08,835
KEEN INSIGHT

688
00:27:08,918 --> 00:27:10,920
Since we all need to eat.

689
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:14,841
Anyway, it's so nice
that you all have titles.

690
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:18,887
I've been wondering what kind of quest
there could be in the mountains.

691
00:27:18,970 --> 00:27:20,305
What about after the sunrise?

692
00:27:20,388 --> 00:27:24,100
Let's talk about the next one
after the Taebaeksan quest is over.

693
00:27:24,184 --> 00:27:25,018
No.

694
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:26,394
"No."

695
00:27:27,687 --> 00:27:30,148
I'd like to go somewhere
I haven't been to.

696
00:27:30,231 --> 00:27:32,275
It's okay as long as it's "san."

697
00:27:32,859 --> 00:27:34,235
"San" Francisco.

698
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:35,737
"San" Francisco.

699
00:27:36,404 --> 00:27:37,947
That place is really nice.

700
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:40,700
-It is.
-It's really nice and warm.

701
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:43,661
Then how about we go to Bu"san" next?

702
00:27:44,287 --> 00:27:45,705
Busan is a really good "san."

703
00:27:46,289 --> 00:27:48,708
When we go to Busan, I'll book a KTX.

704
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:49,959
A BOLD PLEDGE

705
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:50,877
That's good.

706
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:53,630
Hey, there are a lot of stairs
in the KTX station.

707
00:27:53,713 --> 00:27:54,672
The Korail…

708
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,049
It's really tiring.

709
00:27:56,132 --> 00:27:58,301
The stairs in Seoul Station are so steep.

710
00:27:58,385 --> 00:28:00,387
Actually, Ansan is also good.

711
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:03,056
It's nice and close.

712
00:28:03,139 --> 00:28:04,766
My hometown, Ilsan, is good too.

713
00:28:04,849 --> 00:28:06,518
Ilsan? That's a great "san" too.

714
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:09,312
Ilsan's nice.
We can have good <i>kalguksu</i> there.

715
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:10,688
ILSAN'S FAMOUS KALGUKSU TRAIL

716
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:12,399
It's good for the directors too.

717
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:14,692
They can borrow their equipment there.

718
00:28:14,776 --> 00:28:16,069
THERE ARE BROADCAST STATIONS

719
00:28:16,152 --> 00:28:17,862
There are a few broadcast stations there.

720
00:28:18,947 --> 00:28:19,989
There's Yongsan too.

721
00:28:20,073 --> 00:28:22,534
Yongsan is the best. Seriously.

722
00:28:23,326 --> 00:28:25,161
What was that yesterday?

723
00:28:25,245 --> 00:28:26,579
-Biseondae?
-Yes.

724
00:28:26,663 --> 00:28:28,373
If Seoraksan has Biseondae,

725
00:28:28,456 --> 00:28:30,250
it has Soonchunhyang-dae.

726
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:32,627
Near Soonchunhyang University Hospital,

727
00:28:33,128 --> 00:28:36,047
we can have our snacks
at Hannam Intersection.

728
00:28:37,924 --> 00:28:39,217
There are many shelters too.

729
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:41,136
Yes, there are a lot there.

730
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:42,679
It's filled with shelters.

731
00:28:43,221 --> 00:28:45,140
THEBLACKLABEL shelter's there.

732
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:46,433
TARZZAN'S RECORD LABEL

733
00:28:46,516 --> 00:28:47,767
That's a great place.

734
00:28:47,851 --> 00:28:48,685
Yeah, it's good.

735
00:28:49,227 --> 00:28:52,313
Directors, can you each
recommend a mountain?

736
00:28:53,064 --> 00:28:56,484
-Since you all experienced Seoraksan…
-No. Don't.

737
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:57,652
-Director.
-Director.

738
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:59,446
I think he and I are on the same page.

739
00:28:59,946 --> 00:29:00,780
Yongsan, right?

740
00:29:00,864 --> 00:29:01,823
DIRECTOR HONG JEONG-PYO

741
00:29:01,906 --> 00:29:03,158
Because we're on the same team.

742
00:29:03,241 --> 00:29:05,702
-Yes, he and I are on the same team.
-Right.

743
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:07,829
-Those hiking with equipment are
-Yes.

744
00:29:07,912 --> 00:29:09,080
-on the same team as us.
-No.

745
00:29:09,164 --> 00:29:10,832
-That director likes hiking.
-Yes.

746
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:12,500
-We should avoid him.
-Oh, I see.

747
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:14,002
CAMERA DIRECTOR HONG DEOK-HWAN

748
00:29:14,085 --> 00:29:15,378
As for him…

749
00:29:15,462 --> 00:29:17,297
He seems to have a lot to say.

750
00:29:17,380 --> 00:29:18,590
I'm sure he's on our side.

751
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:20,091
AUDIO DIRECTOR KIM SEON-U

752
00:29:20,175 --> 00:29:21,426
I saw the look on his face.

753
00:29:21,509 --> 00:29:24,596
As our diplomat,
why don't you talk to them in private?

754
00:29:24,679 --> 00:29:27,223
-I think I can persuade them easily.
-Okay.

755
00:29:27,307 --> 00:29:28,141
Quite easily.

756
00:29:28,224 --> 00:29:29,934
He's Hong Jeong-pyo, the main director.

757
00:29:30,018 --> 00:29:32,270
He's also the main director
of <i>Culinary Class Wars.</i>

758
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:35,273
Hey, he directed <i>Culinary Class Wars,</i>
and now a hiking show?

759
00:29:35,815 --> 00:29:36,649
Absurd.

760
00:29:37,650 --> 00:29:38,485
From filming food…

761
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:40,361
HE'S FILMING BEAUTIFUL MOUNTAINS INSTEAD

762
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:42,071
Maybe he was duped just like us?

763
00:29:43,031 --> 00:29:44,032
Isn't it possible?

764
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:45,450
REASONABLE DOUBT

765
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:46,493
It is possible.

766
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:49,788
-I'll drive on our way back.
-Okay.

767
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:51,790
RECOVERY STEP 5
MORE PROTEIN INTAKE

768
00:29:52,373 --> 00:29:54,918
Today's schedule is all about eating.

769
00:29:55,001 --> 00:29:56,002
You're right.

770
00:29:56,085 --> 00:29:59,297
We hiked all day long yesterday,
and we're eating all day long today.

771
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:01,090
It's like the National Training Center.

772
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:02,759
We're training too.

773
00:30:02,842 --> 00:30:04,177
It does feel like training.

774
00:30:04,260 --> 00:30:05,094
Exactly.

775
00:30:05,178 --> 00:30:07,388
I think we'll be really motivated
if we do that.

776
00:30:07,472 --> 00:30:09,474
-What?
-Paid money per certain meters.

777
00:30:11,392 --> 00:30:13,436
If we do that,
even Jung-won will never give up.

778
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:16,189
-It's good.
-You know, how about this?

779
00:30:16,272 --> 00:30:18,274
You know the taximeter, right?

780
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:19,609
-Yes.
-Sounds good.

781
00:30:19,692 --> 00:30:22,570
What if each of us wears that
while hiking?

782
00:30:22,654 --> 00:30:24,239
PROPOSAL: HIKING WITH BODY TRACKERS

783
00:30:24,322 --> 00:30:26,533
I don't think
I'll feel good about it though.

784
00:30:27,033 --> 00:30:30,161
Earning money
according to how much we suffer…

785
00:30:30,245 --> 00:30:33,164
But if we use a pedometer,
it'd be 10,000 won per 10,000 steps.

786
00:30:33,248 --> 00:30:34,332
