877
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:26,355
Since it's so early in the morning,

878
00:34:26,856 --> 00:34:28,733
we don't know how our condition will be.

879
00:34:28,816 --> 00:34:29,650
So,

880
00:34:30,234 --> 00:34:33,071
if any of us gets tired,
we'll honestly say, "I need a break."

881
00:34:33,154 --> 00:34:34,363
We'll take a break then.

882
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:36,365
TAKE FREQUENT SHORT BREAKS
WHEN ANYONE WANTS

883
00:34:36,449 --> 00:34:37,450
-Like this?
-Yes.

884
00:34:37,533 --> 00:34:38,785
If we feel tired, just stop.

885
00:34:38,868 --> 00:34:40,286
That's our rule.

886
00:34:40,369 --> 00:34:42,747
Right, that's how
I finished it eventually.

887
00:34:42,830 --> 00:34:45,333
Though I wasn't
intentionally taking breaks.

888
00:34:45,416 --> 00:34:47,627
-Still, you got better.
-Right.

889
00:34:47,710 --> 00:34:49,712
Will Dowoon be taking the lead?

890
00:34:49,796 --> 00:34:51,506
-No, Tarzzan will.
-Tarzzan? Okay.

891
00:34:51,589 --> 00:34:54,008
Slow one, fast one, slow one, fast one.

892
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:56,177
And the directors will be in the middle.

893
00:34:56,260 --> 00:34:57,345
FORMATION RULE DURING HIKE

894
00:34:57,428 --> 00:34:59,222
TARZZAN LEADS, ROTATING PACE

895
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:00,431
That's our rule.

896
00:35:00,515 --> 00:35:02,266
How long will we stay on the top?

897
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:04,018
Assuming we reach it.

898
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:06,854
Is there a shelter on the summit?

899
00:35:06,938 --> 00:35:07,772
No.

900
00:35:07,855 --> 00:35:11,025
Then, since there's no shelter there,
let's climb down when we feel cold.

901
00:35:11,109 --> 00:35:13,402
-Okay, right away.
-We must move when we're cold.

902
00:35:13,486 --> 00:35:15,863
IF IT GETS COLD,
HEAD DOWN WITHOUT LOOKING BACK

903
00:35:16,864 --> 00:35:18,658
"Wait. We need to take a picture here."

904
00:35:18,741 --> 00:35:19,742
We won't.

905
00:35:19,826 --> 00:35:21,577
We won't care. We'll descend.

906
00:35:21,661 --> 00:35:22,495
Good.

907
00:35:22,578 --> 00:35:24,205
DESCEND CLUB'S MEETING ENDS

908
00:35:26,999 --> 00:35:28,126
Hold on. Guys.

909
00:35:28,209 --> 00:35:30,628
-Dowoon, listen.
-No, hold on a second.

910
00:35:30,711 --> 00:35:32,964
There's a dishwasher here.

911
00:35:33,047 --> 00:35:35,383
Why didn't anyone tell me?

912
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:36,300
There is?

913
00:35:36,384 --> 00:35:38,344
But while you did that, we made a plan.

914
00:35:38,427 --> 00:35:39,554
Yes, check it out.

915
00:35:39,637 --> 00:35:41,305
-Just follow our plan.
-Okay.

916
00:35:41,389 --> 00:35:42,223
DOWOON'S VILLAIN ARC

917
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:45,309
This is a plan
for descending and going home early.

918
00:35:45,393 --> 00:35:46,227
Okay.

919
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:47,228
HISTORIC FIRST PLAN

920
00:35:47,311 --> 00:35:49,063
It's our club's first-ever plan.

921
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:50,439
-I'll explain.
-Okay.

922
00:35:50,523 --> 00:35:51,482
We wake up at 2:00 a.m.

923
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,401
-Since we must head out by 2:30 a.m.
-Okay.

924
00:35:53,484 --> 00:35:56,612
And it'll be cold, so we'll climb down
right after watching the sunrise.

925
00:35:56,696 --> 00:35:58,072
Right after…

926
00:35:58,156 --> 00:35:59,073
-the sunrise.
-Okay.

927
00:35:59,866 --> 00:36:01,075
As soon as we see the sun.

928
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:03,244
LEARNING FAST

929
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:04,328
Be like this.

930
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:05,997
READY

931
00:36:06,080 --> 00:36:07,248
Like Usain Bolt.

932
00:36:07,748 --> 00:36:08,708
As soon as we see it.

933
00:36:08,791 --> 00:36:10,459
IMMEDIATELY SWITCHING TO TRAIL RUNNING

934
00:36:10,543 --> 00:36:13,337
What about a penalty? Let's set a rule.

935
00:36:13,421 --> 00:36:16,048
Let's set a rule and a fine.

936
00:36:16,132 --> 00:36:17,383
If we say certain things…

937
00:36:17,466 --> 00:36:19,719
-We can't say something negative.
-Okay.

938
00:36:19,802 --> 00:36:22,221
-Nothing negative.
-Let's stay positive tomorrow.

939
00:36:22,305 --> 00:36:24,056
-How much should the fine be?
-The fine?

940
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:25,558
Let's make it big. 100,000 won.

941
00:36:25,641 --> 00:36:27,393
But I think we need a limit.

942
00:36:27,476 --> 00:36:31,105
If you have to pay 100,000 won
whenever you say something negative,

943
00:36:31,189 --> 00:36:33,232
I think once our show is over,

944
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:35,484
Car-the might have to sell his car.

945
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:37,320
THEN HE BECOMES JUST "THE GARDEN"

946
00:36:37,403 --> 00:36:38,404
So negative.

947
00:36:38,487 --> 00:36:40,489
So how about we pay a fine just once?

948
00:36:40,573 --> 00:36:44,035
I mean, you just need to
pay a 100,000-won fine per one hike.

949
00:36:44,118 --> 00:36:45,369
I think that's better.

950
00:36:45,453 --> 00:36:46,537
Well…

951
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:48,039
Should we raise the fine?

952
00:36:48,122 --> 00:36:49,832
-The fine…
-Raise it.

953
00:36:49,916 --> 00:36:51,167
-It's per hike.
-Right.

954
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:52,877
-Make it 300,000 won.
-Good.

955
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:57,965
DESCEND CLUB'S
FIRST HIKING PLAN COMPLETED

956
00:36:58,049 --> 00:37:00,760
He and I are going to sleep
in hiking clothes.

957
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:02,094
LAUGHING

958
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:05,556
You do that when you go to the ski resort
so you can leave right away.

959
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:06,724
BEDTIME APPROACHES

960
00:37:06,807 --> 00:37:07,642
That's a good idea.

961
00:37:07,725 --> 00:37:09,352
AND THE NIGHT DEEPENS

962
00:37:13,439 --> 00:37:14,857
I don't want to go hiking tomorrow.

963
00:37:14,941 --> 00:37:16,567
THEY DON'T WANT TO GO TO BED

964
00:37:16,651 --> 00:37:17,944
I want to wake up at 8:00 a.m.

965
00:37:18,027 --> 00:37:21,989
It's nice to chat with people
speaking the same language.

966
00:37:22,073 --> 00:37:23,199
-It is.
-Right.

967
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:25,326
My ways to relieve stress

968
00:37:25,409 --> 00:37:28,120
-are things like basketball and gym.
-Right.

969
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:29,413
TOPIC 1: HOW TO RELIEVE STRESS

970
00:37:29,497 --> 00:37:31,958
And finding your own ways to do that
is the smart thing to do.

971
00:37:32,041 --> 00:37:33,793
-Right.
-Wow, you're incredible.

972
00:37:33,876 --> 00:37:35,920
Since I wanted to perform on stage,

973
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:38,798
I needed to learn how to dance.

974
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:40,383
TOPIC 2: DREAMS AND JOBS

975
00:37:40,466 --> 00:37:41,801
So I started modern dance.

976
00:37:41,884 --> 00:37:45,304
Now that I've talked with you guys
since we started filming,

977
00:37:45,388 --> 00:37:46,847
I'm glad I decided to do this.

978
00:37:46,931 --> 00:37:49,767
There are many things I can't do
since I'm timid.

979
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:51,102
TOPIC 3: EMOTIONAL CONFESSIONS

980
00:37:51,185 --> 00:37:52,645
So people around me were surprised.

981
00:37:52,728 --> 00:37:55,731
NOSTALGIC GAMES

982
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:59,151
AND NOSTALGIC DRAMA SHOWS

983
00:38:02,029 --> 00:38:04,240
TIME HAS FLOWN

984
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:07,827
YAWNING

985
00:38:08,619 --> 00:38:10,162
Now, let's go to bed.

986
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:11,372
Let's try to sleep.

987
00:38:11,455 --> 00:38:13,082
What time is it?

988
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:14,292
It's 12:00 a.m. now?

989
00:38:14,375 --> 00:38:16,711
ONLY 2 HOURS LEFT UNTIL WAKE-UP TIME

990
00:38:28,264 --> 00:38:30,850
THEY GO TO BED FOR REAL

991
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:33,894
TIME PASSES BY FAST

992
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:40,526
CURRENT TIME

993
00:38:43,154 --> 00:38:44,322
We need to get up.

994
00:38:44,405 --> 00:38:45,740
-What?
-We need to get up.

995
00:38:46,574 --> 00:38:47,408
It's 2:00 a.m.

996
00:38:48,117 --> 00:38:50,494
<i>You woke up at 2:00 a.m., right?</i>

997
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:51,412
<i>How was it?</i>

998
00:38:51,495 --> 00:38:52,538
Well, it was hard.

999
00:38:53,539 --> 00:38:55,916
Because of a drama filming schedule,

1000
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:59,462
the earliest I had to wake up
was 2:30 a.m.

1001
00:38:59,545 --> 00:39:01,464
And I broke the record this time.

1002
00:39:01,964 --> 00:39:02,840
Well…

1003
00:39:02,923 --> 00:39:03,883
Thank you.

1004
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:09,680
CHAE-MIN GETS UP

1005
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:15,144
CAR, THE GARDEN GETS UP

1006
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:16,437
Dowoon.

1007
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:17,355
Yes?

1008
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:19,398
-Oh, you didn't sleep?
-No.

1009
00:39:19,482 --> 00:39:20,649
Did you?

1010
00:39:20,733 --> 00:39:22,401
-A little.
-Wow.

1011
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:25,279
DOWOON COULDN'T SLEEP A WINK

1012
00:39:25,988 --> 00:39:28,115
Gosh, will we be able to hike?

1013
00:39:29,116 --> 00:39:30,451
Seriously.

1014
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:31,702
We'll have to.

1015
00:39:31,786 --> 00:39:33,329
It feels like a moment ago.

1016
00:39:35,164 --> 00:39:36,707
LASTLY, TARZZAN

1017
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:40,169
EVERYONE IS UP

1018
00:39:41,587 --> 00:39:45,758
NONE OF THEM SLEPT PROPERLY

1019
00:39:47,009 --> 00:39:48,094
I'm mad already.

1020
00:39:48,177 --> 00:39:50,471
SAYING SOMETHING NICE RIGHT AWAY

1021
00:39:51,180 --> 00:39:53,599
-I'm pissed off.
-It felt like just a nap.

1022
00:39:55,309 --> 00:39:57,603
BUT HE GETS CHANGED THE FASTEST

1023
00:39:59,271 --> 00:40:01,524
WHAT DO YOU THINK YOUR WEAKNESS IS?

1024
00:40:01,607 --> 00:40:02,441
I'M IMPATIENT

1025
00:40:03,526 --> 00:40:06,028
TARZZAN WEARS AN ORANGE BALACLAVA

1026
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:08,697
You're bundled up today.

1027
00:40:08,781 --> 00:40:09,615
Yes.

1028
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:11,867
Apparently, it's so windy.

1029
00:40:12,451 --> 00:40:15,663
WIND SPEED IN TAEBAEKSAN
"A LITTLE STRONG" TO "STRONG"

1030
00:40:15,746 --> 00:40:18,999
IT'S GOING TO FEEL STRONGER
BECAUSE OF THE OPEN RIDGES

1031
00:40:20,584 --> 00:40:22,837
SPACING OUT

1032
00:40:23,421 --> 00:40:26,507
TRYING TO WAKE UP
WHILE FOLDING UP THE BEDDING

1033
00:40:27,341 --> 00:40:29,635
UPON WAKING UP, HE TAKES SUPPLEMENTS

1034
00:40:30,219 --> 00:40:31,846
AND SOME MORE

1035
00:40:31,929 --> 00:40:34,807
HABIT FOR STAMINA
TAKING JUICE AND SUPPLEMENTS

1036
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:39,520
QUICKLY NOURISHING HIS SKIN AS WELL

1037
00:40:40,438 --> 00:40:41,939
Do we need this?

1038
00:40:42,022 --> 00:40:44,275
Yes, we should wear them from the start.

1039
00:40:44,775 --> 00:40:47,653
GAITERS PROTECT LEGS FROM THE COLD
