1284
00:53:41,551 --> 00:53:42,636
-Jung-won.
-Yes?

1285
00:53:42,719 --> 00:53:45,263
This chair here is not wet.
You can sit here.

1286
00:53:45,347 --> 00:53:47,349
No, I think it's better not to sit down.

1287
00:53:49,601 --> 00:53:50,936
Anyone want a drink?

1288
00:53:51,728 --> 00:53:53,438
I got a sports drink.

1289
00:53:54,940 --> 00:53:55,774
Thanks.

1290
00:53:56,524 --> 00:53:58,777
HERE COMES HELPER DOWOON AGAIN

1291
00:53:59,402 --> 00:54:00,403
I'll have a sip too.

1292
00:54:00,487 --> 00:54:01,905
Everyone, take a sip.

1293
00:54:03,573 --> 00:54:06,284
AFTER THE YOUNGEST TAKES A SIP

1294
00:54:06,910 --> 00:54:09,537
<i>I also said this</i>
<i>when I decided to do this show.</i>

1295
00:54:10,288 --> 00:54:11,790
<i>I want to be helpful.</i>

1296
00:54:11,873 --> 00:54:14,626
Honestly, I'm not good
at making others laugh.

1297
00:54:14,709 --> 00:54:18,421
I'm not good at making jokes
on the spot like Jung-won.

1298
00:54:18,505 --> 00:54:21,591
So, I tried
to look after the others, at least.

1299
00:54:21,675 --> 00:54:23,927
I think I found the right role for me.

1300
00:54:24,803 --> 00:54:27,472
By the way,
it seems your backpack is quite heavy.

1301
00:54:28,056 --> 00:54:29,849
-Is it?
-What did you put in?

1302
00:54:29,933 --> 00:54:31,935
-Just…
-Did you put in the pots?

1303
00:54:32,018 --> 00:54:33,228
-Yes.
-The pots?

1304
00:54:33,311 --> 00:54:34,854
THE SAME BACKPACK USED IN SEORAKSAN

1305
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:37,440
Why don't you give them to me?
I'm not carrying much.

1306
00:54:37,524 --> 00:54:39,317
But the backpack isn't the problem.

1307
00:54:39,401 --> 00:54:40,777
Then, your legs?

1308
00:54:40,860 --> 00:54:41,695
Yes.

1309
00:54:43,113 --> 00:54:44,948
And we're not fully awake yet.

1310
00:54:45,031 --> 00:54:46,449
-Yes, that too.
-We're still foggy.

1311
00:54:46,533 --> 00:54:47,367
So foggy.

1312
00:54:47,450 --> 00:54:49,035
We're just walking.

1313
00:54:49,536 --> 00:54:50,537
If you look here,

1314
00:54:50,620 --> 00:54:53,498
we've come one kilometer
from Yuilsa Parking Lot,

1315
00:54:53,581 --> 00:54:56,084
and Cheonjedan is three kilometers away.

1316
00:54:56,167 --> 00:54:57,836
<i>We're a quarter of the way, then.</i>

1317
00:54:57,919 --> 00:54:59,421
<i>-So we have 3 km to go.</i>
<i>-Okay.</i>

1318
00:54:59,504 --> 00:55:00,880
2.7 KM LEFT UNTIL JANGGUNBONG PEAK

1319
00:55:01,506 --> 00:55:03,967
1 HOUR 29 MINUTES UNTIL SUNRISE

1320
00:55:04,050 --> 00:55:04,884
Let's go.

1321
00:55:05,427 --> 00:55:06,261
Okay.

1322
00:55:06,344 --> 00:55:07,971
We go when you go.

1323
00:55:08,054 --> 00:55:08,930
Right.

1324
00:55:10,140 --> 00:55:12,642
DESCEND CLUB RULES
BREAKS: LESS THAN 5 MINUTES

1325
00:55:15,061 --> 00:55:16,771
We're already a quarter of the way.

1326
00:55:16,855 --> 00:55:17,731
Right.

1327
00:55:22,402 --> 00:55:26,072
LEAD: CAR, THE GARDEN

1328
00:55:26,156 --> 00:55:28,742
MIDDLE 1: TARZZAN

1329
00:55:28,825 --> 00:55:31,077
MIDDLE 2: CHAE-MIN

1330
00:55:31,161 --> 00:55:33,496
TAIL: DOWOON

1331
00:55:34,789 --> 00:55:41,755
NOW THE PACE SEEMS PERFECT

1332
00:55:50,430 --> 00:55:51,765
I feel hot now.

1333
00:55:52,348 --> 00:55:54,350
I'm starting to feel warm now.

1334
00:55:54,434 --> 00:55:55,268
Right.

1335
00:55:55,351 --> 00:55:57,103
I should take off a layer.

1336
00:55:57,187 --> 00:55:58,313
-Right?
-Yes.

1337
00:56:01,649 --> 00:56:03,359
Jung-won, it's nothing funny, but…

1338
00:56:04,277 --> 00:56:07,655
Do you know Russell, a US sports brand?

1339
00:56:07,739 --> 00:56:09,199
-Russell?
-Russell.

1340
00:56:09,282 --> 00:56:10,116
I don't.

1341
00:56:10,617 --> 00:56:13,161
WHEN CLIMBING A SNOW MOUNTAIN,

1342
00:56:13,244 --> 00:56:15,789
THE LEAD PLOWS THROUGH SNOW TO MAKE A PATH

1343
00:56:15,872 --> 00:56:16,873
It's a hiking term.

1344
00:56:17,916 --> 00:56:18,917
Just go.

1345
00:56:19,876 --> 00:56:21,753
Russell, my foot.

1346
00:56:21,836 --> 00:56:23,797
I was taken aback. I got goosebumps.

1347
00:56:24,297 --> 00:56:25,131
Seriously.

1348
00:56:25,215 --> 00:56:26,883
Do you know what he said to me?

1349
00:56:26,966 --> 00:56:27,842
What is it?

1350
00:56:27,926 --> 00:56:29,260
"It's nothing funny, but…"

1351
00:56:29,344 --> 00:56:30,595
TELLING ON THE DOCENT

1352
00:56:30,678 --> 00:56:32,472
"Do you know the brand Russell?"

1353
00:56:32,555 --> 00:56:34,724
"Stepping on snow is called Russell."

1354
00:56:34,808 --> 00:56:35,892
-Stepping on snow?
-Yes.

1355
00:56:35,975 --> 00:56:37,602
I mean, who cares, right?

1356
00:56:38,353 --> 00:56:40,063
BADMOUTHING HIM SO OPENLY

1357
00:56:40,146 --> 00:56:41,272
I'm dumbfounded.

1358
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:44,025
THANKS TO THAT, HE FEELS HOT

1359
00:56:44,109 --> 00:56:45,777
He's getting negative.

1360
00:56:45,860 --> 00:56:47,946
Gosh, this is bad.

1361
00:56:48,780 --> 00:56:49,989
Do you know Cha Jung-sook?

1362
00:56:51,032 --> 00:56:52,951
She's my aunt. Ms. Cha Jung-sook.

1363
00:56:53,535 --> 00:56:54,369
Hey.

1364
00:56:54,452 --> 00:56:55,620
Why don't we

1365
00:56:55,703 --> 00:56:57,622
-take a break?
-To take off a layer?

1366
00:56:57,705 --> 00:56:59,332
I should take off some clothes.

1367
00:56:59,833 --> 00:57:00,708
I'm feeling hot.

1368
00:57:00,792 --> 00:57:03,670
A BREAK TO TAKE OFF CLOTHES

1369
00:57:03,753 --> 00:57:07,715
While we're at it,
let's split what you're carrying.

1370
00:57:07,799 --> 00:57:09,092
Seriously, it's heavy.

1371
00:57:09,175 --> 00:57:10,301
No, the bag is really fine.

1372
00:57:10,385 --> 00:57:13,429
It's just that
my thighs were hurting earlier.

1373
00:57:13,513 --> 00:57:15,723
-It was really your thighs?
-Yes. I'm fine now.

1374
00:57:15,807 --> 00:57:17,350
But still, it's really heavy.

1375
00:57:17,433 --> 00:57:19,269
FEELING THE WEIGHT

1376
00:57:19,352 --> 00:57:21,688
I didn't even feel the backpack, no lie.

1377
00:57:22,272 --> 00:57:24,441
My thighs hurt so annoyingly earlier.

1378
00:57:24,524 --> 00:57:25,650
They still hurt?

1379
00:57:25,733 --> 00:57:27,485
It was so steep from the start.

1380
00:57:27,569 --> 00:57:29,237
-It was.
-True.

1381
00:57:29,320 --> 00:57:30,155
I'm fine now.

1382
00:57:30,864 --> 00:57:32,323
Wow, so positive.

1383
00:57:33,616 --> 00:57:34,951
You guys are not tired?

1384
00:57:35,034 --> 00:57:35,910
I am.

1385
00:57:35,994 --> 00:57:36,870
-Right?
-Yes.

1386
00:57:36,953 --> 00:57:38,163
I'm not the only one, right?

1387
00:57:38,872 --> 00:57:40,957
-Apparently, it'll get better.
-What?

1388
00:57:41,040 --> 00:57:42,417
A POSITIVE MAN

1389
00:57:42,500 --> 00:57:44,752
A "NAH"GATIVE MAN

1390
00:57:44,836 --> 00:57:46,671
It felt like climbing a ski slope.

1391
00:57:47,338 --> 00:57:48,840
ALL READY

1392
00:57:48,923 --> 00:57:49,966
You got changed.

1393
00:57:50,467 --> 00:57:52,385
You look like a spaceman.

1394
00:57:52,469 --> 00:57:53,344
Right?

1395
00:57:55,138 --> 00:57:55,972
SPACEMAN PERFORMANCE

1396
00:57:56,055 --> 00:57:57,432
It looks like you're on the moon.

1397
00:57:57,932 --> 00:57:59,851
Wow, you can do those moves.

1398
00:58:03,021 --> 00:58:04,981
Did you know you can change the color?

1399
00:58:06,357 --> 00:58:07,525
A HEADLAMP PERFORMANCE

1400
00:58:07,609 --> 00:58:08,610
It changed with a button.

1401
00:58:08,693 --> 00:58:10,737
-Hey, Tarzzan.
-Yes?

1402
00:58:10,820 --> 00:58:12,238
Don't enjoy hiking too much.

1403
00:58:13,573 --> 00:58:15,325
-Wait.
-You're enjoying it too much.

1404
00:58:15,408 --> 00:58:17,076
That's not right for our club.

1405
00:58:17,744 --> 00:58:19,287
You're enjoying it too much.

1406
00:58:20,079 --> 00:58:21,039
Take it easy.

1407
00:58:22,916 --> 00:58:26,127
I think Jung-won
is going back and forth right now.

1408
00:58:26,211 --> 00:58:28,213
That's enough. Don't enjoy it too much.

1409
00:58:28,296 --> 00:58:29,756
HE DOESN'T CARE

1410
00:58:29,839 --> 00:58:32,342
It's not exactly being negative.

1411
00:58:32,425 --> 00:58:34,385
Right. It sounds like… advice?

1412
00:58:34,469 --> 00:58:35,303
Yes, advice.

1413
00:58:36,387 --> 00:58:38,014
Maybe advice to himself?

1414
00:58:38,097 --> 00:58:38,973
It's advice.

1415
00:58:39,766 --> 00:58:42,602
CURRENT LOCATION

1416
00:58:42,685 --> 00:58:45,146
MOVING AGAIN

1417
00:58:45,230 --> 00:58:47,440
1 HOUR 12 MINUTES UNTIL SUNRISE

1418
00:58:48,024 --> 00:58:52,695
ENTERING THE SECTION WITH MORE SNOW

1419
00:58:52,779 --> 00:58:54,239
Wow, it's all snow?

1420
00:58:54,739 --> 00:58:56,491
-It's insane.
-I want to jump there.

1421
00:58:56,574 --> 00:58:58,493
-What?
-I want to jump there.

1422
00:58:58,576 --> 00:58:59,410
Me too.

1423
00:58:59,494 --> 00:59:01,496
SNOWY HILL NEXT TO THE TRAIL

1424
00:59:02,830 --> 00:59:05,458
It's all snow.
Did someone push it here on purpose?

1425
00:59:06,709 --> 00:59:08,336
I think it was naturally formed.

1426
00:59:09,337 --> 00:59:10,964
Since people have stepped on snow here.

1427
00:59:11,047 --> 00:59:12,257
I think so.

1428
00:59:14,050 --> 00:59:19,222
THE SNOWY MOUNTAIN
IS ALSO BEAUTIFUL IN DAYLIGHT

1429
00:59:21,015 --> 00:59:23,726
By the way, sparkling snow
looks so beautiful.

1430
00:59:23,810 --> 00:59:26,312
-Right.
-When you shine the light on it.

1431
00:59:26,396 --> 00:59:27,855
It looks like diamonds.

1432
00:59:34,195 --> 00:59:35,446
There's a lot of snow.

1433
00:59:41,411 --> 00:59:42,412
It's so snowy.

1434
00:59:45,123 --> 00:59:47,917
By the way,
Jung-won is climbing pretty well.

1435
00:59:56,759 --> 00:59:59,429
CAR-THE'S CAM

1436
01:00:17,322 --> 01:00:20,867
Walking, following someone like this…

1437
01:00:21,743 --> 01:00:23,119
It's been ages.

1438
01:00:27,040 --> 01:00:29,125
When else would I follow someone?

1439
01:00:30,209 --> 01:00:33,421
Right? You rarely follow someone
after you become an adult.

1440
01:00:35,506 --> 01:00:40,178
But walking
following the producer's lantern light,

1441
01:00:40,887 --> 01:00:42,138
it's kind of fun.

1442
01:00:49,228 --> 01:00:51,606
This has been on my mind
while filming the show.

1443
01:00:52,732 --> 01:00:55,943
I mostly do what I can do
or what I want to do

1444
01:00:56,027 --> 01:00:57,945
these days.

1445
01:01:00,823 --> 01:01:04,327
So there aren't many situations
where I have to follow someone.

1446
01:01:04,410 --> 01:01:07,205
Because I only go to places I've been to

1447
01:01:08,748 --> 01:01:10,249
or places I can go,

1448
01:01:11,459 --> 01:01:13,002
not anywhere I don't know.

1449
01:01:14,003 --> 01:01:17,548
So I don't need to follow anyone.
I don't need anyone to guide me.

1450
01:01:18,508 --> 01:01:19,634
<i>But in the mountains,</i>

1451
01:01:20,885 --> 01:01:22,261
<i>I didn't know the path.</i>

1452
01:01:23,888 --> 01:01:27,392
<i>So I had to rely</i>
<i>on the producer's lantern light.</i>

1453
01:01:30,853 --> 01:01:33,314
It felt like I was young again.

1454
01:01:35,400 --> 01:01:36,651
I felt vulnerable.

1455
01:01:36,734 --> 01:01:39,445
I was actually weak. Yes.

1456
01:01:46,911 --> 01:01:49,914
When I worked at a company
or at a factory,

1457
01:01:50,665 --> 01:01:52,417
I used to walk a lot.

1458
01:01:53,292 --> 01:01:54,877
It wasn't to save money.

1459
01:01:56,254 --> 01:01:57,547
I just walked a lot.

1460
01:01:58,798 --> 01:02:00,550
I just walked without thinking.

1461
01:02:01,843 --> 01:02:05,263
In winter, when I went to work,
there would be a lot of snow

1462
01:02:05,346 --> 01:02:06,472
on my way to work.

1463
01:02:07,640 --> 01:02:08,641
It feels like that.

1464
01:02:16,774 --> 01:02:17,942
There were such days.

1465
01:02:23,239 --> 01:02:25,533
Now I act like I'm all that. Right?

1466
01:02:36,002 --> 01:02:37,253
Can I fart loudly?

1467
01:02:37,795 --> 01:02:39,380
Fart? Sure, go ahead.

1468
01:02:39,881 --> 01:02:41,883
-I did.
-I farted a lot, to be honest.

1469
01:02:42,717 --> 01:02:43,551
What?

1470
01:02:44,802 --> 01:02:45,720
Jung-won!

1471
01:02:46,721 --> 01:02:47,930
Should we wait a little?

1472
01:02:48,014 --> 01:02:49,015
Sure.

1473
01:02:51,142 --> 01:02:53,603
You're suddenly in good form.

1474
01:02:54,187 --> 01:02:57,315
THE YOUNGER ONES CATCH UP

1475
01:02:57,398 --> 01:02:59,025
It's uphill from now on.

1476
01:02:59,650 --> 01:03:02,487
CURRENT LOCATION

1477
01:03:02,570 --> 01:03:08,743
CAR-THE, DOWOON, TARZZAN, CHAE-MIN

1478
01:03:09,368 --> 01:03:11,871
Wait a second.
I think the sun's about to rise.

1479
01:03:11,954 --> 01:03:12,789
What?

1480
01:03:13,289 --> 01:03:16,417
You're right.
The sky's beginning to lighten.

1481
01:03:17,001 --> 01:03:17,835
What?

1482
01:03:17,919 --> 01:03:19,253
The sun's about to rise.

1483
01:03:19,337 --> 01:03:20,421
Really?

1484
01:03:20,505 --> 01:03:22,048
I think we should hurry up.

1485
01:03:22,924 --> 01:03:24,050
Let's go.

1486
01:03:28,513 --> 01:03:29,806
I think we're almost there.

1487
01:03:29,889 --> 01:03:31,933
You're right. It's getting bright.

1488
01:03:34,936 --> 01:03:36,187
What time is it?

1489
01:03:38,439 --> 01:03:39,774
Maybe 6…

1490
01:03:40,316 --> 01:03:41,609
Maybe 6:40 a.m.?

1491
01:03:41,692 --> 01:03:43,319
It should be around that.

1492
01:03:43,402 --> 01:03:46,197
CLIMBING THE STEEP UPHILL TRAIL

1493
01:03:46,280 --> 01:03:47,365
Are we taking a zipline?

1494
01:03:47,949 --> 01:03:50,618
Do you want to take a break
in that rest area

1495
01:03:50,701 --> 01:03:51,536
or keep going?

1496
01:03:51,619 --> 01:03:53,913
-We have to go.
-Let's just go without a break.

1497
01:03:53,996 --> 01:03:56,207
It's 6:44 a.m. now.

1498
01:03:56,290 --> 01:03:59,669
52 MINUTES UNTIL SUNRISE

1499
01:03:59,752 --> 01:04:01,879
The rest of the course takes an hour.

1500
01:04:01,963 --> 01:04:05,675
THEY ARE 8 MINUTES SHORT

1501
01:04:05,758 --> 01:04:08,386
THE HIGHER THE ELEVATION
THE DEEPER THE SNOW

1502
01:04:08,469 --> 01:04:09,637
Is this really a trail?

1503
01:04:09,720 --> 01:04:11,472
We're literally making a path.

1504
01:04:13,140 --> 01:04:13,975
Geez.

1505
01:04:14,934 --> 01:04:16,853
We're almost there. Hang in there.

1506
01:04:16,936 --> 01:04:19,605
No, I can't. Let me rest
for just 30 seconds.

1507
01:04:19,689 --> 01:04:22,358
When you're so tired,
you get mentally weak too.

1508
01:04:22,441 --> 01:04:23,317
So…

1509
01:04:23,401 --> 01:04:25,278
It feels like playing tag with the sun.

1510
01:04:25,361 --> 01:04:26,737
It's getting brighter.

1511
01:04:26,821 --> 01:04:29,740
<i>As the sky began to lighten,</i>
<i>I was getting anxious.</i>

1512
01:04:29,824 --> 01:04:31,868
I thought, "After we've come this far,

1513
01:04:31,951 --> 01:04:34,036
<i>if we fail, it'll be so disappointing."</i>

1514
01:04:34,120 --> 01:04:36,956
<i>I mean, we even sacrificed sleep for this.</i>

1515
01:04:37,039 --> 01:04:38,708
-Producer.
-Yes?

1516
01:04:38,791 --> 01:04:40,334
-I need…
-A break?

1517
01:04:40,418 --> 01:04:42,128
It's really bad.

1518
01:04:42,211 --> 01:04:43,754
-Your legs?
-Here.

1519
01:04:43,838 --> 01:04:45,590
-Really?
-It feels like they're tearing.

1520
01:05:39,644 --> 01:05:41,646
Subtitle translation by: Wayne Ryu
